      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-68020",
      ":question/problem": "The table below shows the relationship between the number of revolutions $r$ that a carousel at a fair completes in $m$ minutes.\n\n| Minutes $(m)$ | Revolutions $(r)$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $1$ | $6$ |\n| $3$ | $18$ |\n| $5$ | $30$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. There is a proportional relationship between $r$ and $m$.\n2. There is **not** a proportional relationship between $r$ and $m$.\n3. The constant of proportionality is $18$."
    },
