      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-68170",
      ":question/problem": "Rick is driving on a highway. The relationship between the time $t$ (in minutes) he drives and the distance $d$ (in miles) he covers is shown in the table below.\n\n| Minutes ($t$) | Miles ($d$) |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $4$ | $3$ |\n| $8$ | $6$ |\n| $12$ | $9$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. There is **not** a proportional relationship between $d$ and $t$.\n2. There is a proportional relationship between $d$ and $t$.\n3. The constant of proportionality is $\\frac{3}{4}$."
    }
